=== Classical adaptor baseline: libsecp256k1-zkp ecdsa_adaptor ===
(same machine/compiler as bench_las3; 2000 iterations/op; reused
 production implementation - only this timing harness is ours)

  KeyGen / statement gen     34.66 us
  Sign   (ECDSA)            46.32 us
  Verify (ECDSA)            67.62 us
  PreSign   (encrypt)      211.60 us
  PreVerify (verify)       271.32 us
  Adapt     (decrypt)        3.63 us
  Ext       (recover)       34.82 us

  sizes: pk/statement 33 B (compressed) | sk/witness 32 B |
         sig 64 B compact (70 B DER) | pre-sig (adaptor) 162 B

  note: the 162 B pre-signature is a syntactically distinct object
  (ECDSA sig + DLEQ proof); LAS pre-sigs share the signature format
  and fail Verify cryptographically. Constant-time production code -
  comparison flatters the classical side vs reference-style LAS.
=== classical baseline OK ===
